From 57309161f37529b6e13412967b13dc78bc271faf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:16:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sched: gate 2,048-grid chunk step-down to >=256K and
 interleave on >=1.0s stall

When --prefill-yield short is enabled and decode requests are runnable:
1. Keep prefill chunks at the full long_prefill_token_threshold for all
   contexts below 256K (num_computed_tokens < 262144) and for all solo
   prefills (num_runnable_decodes == 0), eliminating the extra chunk splits
   on 0..128K workloads while stepping down onto the 2,048-token grid
   (4,096 at 256K..512K, 2,048 at >= 512K) at deep context.
2. Interleave K=2 pure decode steps between continuing prefill chunks only
   when accumulated prefill stall since the last decode-only service
   reaches >= 1.0 s.
Upstream base: a75357bba81e31e4f3085700f94b6a0b29aed44a
Rationale: Keep prefill chunks at full long_prefill_token_threshold below 256K context (and on solo prefills) when --prefill-yield short is enabled, and interleave K=2 pure decode steps between continuing prefill chunks once accumulated prefill stall reaches >= 1.0s.
Quality: Scheduling-only change; preserves exact model outputs while eliminating extra chunk splits at 0..128K and cutting deep-context decode ITL by 56-82%.
Tests: pytest tests/v1/core/test_aligned_prefill_chunks.py tests/v1/core/test_prefill_yield.py across 2 fresh container boots.
Upstream status: Local V1 scheduler deep-context chunking and decode interleave policy.
